  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gaindan Lal vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 1 December, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "The instant anticipatory bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicant, Gaindan Lal, with a prayer to release him on bail in Case Crime No. 396 of 2020, under Sections- 420, 272, 273 I.P.C., 57 and 58 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, Police Station- Bahjoi, District- Sambhal. There is allegation in the F.I.R. that the son of the applicant and co-accused, Sachin, was involved in making adulterated milk.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant was not arrested on the spot. He has been implicated only because of the conduct of his son. The applicant has no criminal history to his credit. He has definite apprehension that he may be arrested by the police any time. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for anticipatory bail of the applicant. Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail for limited period in this case considering the exceptions considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2609 of 2020.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant was not arrested on the spot. He has been implicated only because of the conduct of his son. The applicant has no criminal history to his credit. He has definite apprehension that he may be arrested by the police any time. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for anticipatory bail of the applicant.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail for limited period in this case considering the exceptions considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No. 2609 of 2020."
